An Irq's description tells the bits it is armed with, not those it may signal.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -972,7 +972,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) int cap_info(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t *a
         /* What the bind's capability may signal, zero once the notification was taken, and never what is armed. */
         const struct irq *irq = (const struct irq *)cap_object(cap);
         arg[2] = irq->line;
-        arg[3] = irq->may;
+        arg[3] = irq->bits;
         arg[4] = line_is_timer(irq->line);
         break;
     }
